From: Thomas Skovlund Hansen <thomas@skovlund.dev>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 04:25:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] docs(conventions): rules encode intent; trim, update and add
 releases and generation

The general conventions open with how to read them: follow the intent,
not the letter; nothing is maintained for its own sake; generate over
hand-maintain. Testing asks for the critical paths and tests that each
catch a regression, not a coverage percentage. The gate is tool-agnostic
instead of `make` targets, the per-archetype table no longer names repos
or hypothesis, retries allow a bounded reconnect, and the branch-and-PR
flow with squash merges is the default. Releases are tags with notes
drafted from commits and curated on GitHub; there is no changelog file.
Docs state what the code does not and never carry drifting counts.
AGENTS.md needs no CLAUDE.md symlink now that Claude Code reads it;
this repo's own symlink goes too. Python and TypeScript modules add the
no-escape-hatch and docstring-semantics rules.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
